 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Affine isomorphism criterion from topology and local rings",
 "statement": "Let $\\varphi:A\\to B$ be a homomorphism of commutative rings. Suppose the induced map $\\operatorname{Spec}B\\to\\operatorname{Spec}A$ [def-weil-affine-spectrum] is a homeomorphism and, for every prime $\\mathfrak q\\subset B$, the canonical map of prime localizations [def-weil-pbc-localization-at-prime] $A_{\\varphi^{-1}(\\mathfrak q)}\\to B_{\\mathfrak q}$ is an isomorphism. Then $\\varphi$ is an isomorphism of rings.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/stacks-project/proetale.tex",
  "place": "Tag 096L, lemma-local-isomorphism-fully-faithful, corollary for an algebra identifying local rings with spectrum homeomorphic to the base; Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/OpenImmersion.lean:524 and Morphisms/IsIso.lean:58"
 },
